<section
  class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[var(--container-max)] px-4 py-16"
  aria-labelledby="why-heading"
>
  <div class="max-w-[60ch]">
    <h2 id="why-heading" class="type-headline text-foreground-strong">
      Why this exists
    </h2>
    <p class="type-body mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
      The frames that make Arabic and Islamic art feel finished are just a few concentric
      lines in the right proportions. Getting them right otherwise means opening a design
      tool, starting a new file, and nudging rectangles for twenty minutes.
    </p>
    <p class="type-body mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
      Here it is a few numbers, a colour and, if you like, a pattern. The presets are named
      recipes &mdash; Double Rule, Gilded Hairline, Heavy Band, Triple Thread, Star Band,
      Kufic Key &mdash; and every value in them stays editable the moment you apply one.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
